The ball is now lifted above the floor and dropped so that it falls vertically, as illustrated in Fig. 3.2.

{{figure:figure_3_2.png}}

Just before contact with the floor, the ball has velocity $6.2\text{ m s}^{-1}$ downwards. The ball bounces from the floor and its velocity just after losing contact with the floor is $2.5\text{ m s}^{-1}$ upwards. The ball is in contact with the floor for $0.12\text{ s}$.
